 "question": "Why do the six paper books hold nothing, when `exits.evaluate` has honoured `min_normal_hold_sessions` since 2026-09-05?",
 "answer": "Because the minimum hold was never the binding constraint. `HARD_RISK_LIMIT` is always legal and is checked ABOVE the hold, and the stop widths were profile constants unrelated to the volatility of the names the books were actually buying. On hack6 the stop sat at 0.98 daily standard deviations of its own holdings, so 56.3% of entries were stopped out before session 10 of a 21-session thesis.",
 "method": "For every name in the 2026-09-07 sealed book, daily Alpaca closes (adjustment=all, SIP feed) from 2024-01-01. For every entry point the running return from entry is walked forward and the first session at which it touches -stop is recorded. P(stop before hold) is the share of entry points whose first touch falls at or before the contract's minimum hold; P(survive horizon) is the share never touched inside the horizon. This measures the EXIT RULE against the book's own names. It is not a strategy backtest and carries no return claim.",
