 "caveats": [
  "Path dependence is measured on CLOSES only; an intraday touch of the stop is not observed here, so P(stop before hold) is a LOWER bound on how often the stop fires.",
  "The sample is roughly 20 months of one regime. It bounds nothing about 2008.",
  "hack4's sealed book was EMPTY on 2026-09-07 (requires_catalyst=true, rank_distinct_values=0), so its row is DECLARED, not measured on its own names.",
  "hack5 is a long-premium book: the stop charge and the true bound are different numbers and both are reported.",
  "This receipt is about the EXIT RULE's ability to let a thesis run. It says nothing about whether any of these books has an edge, and no edge is claimed here."
 ],
